( series-stats.tal — order statistics + mean as a ROM. Integers, no floats. )
( The second gate of the REDUCE-A-SERIES class [spearman.tal was the first]. )
(                                                                                        )
( WHY: the doctrine's standing quantitative claims are order statistics — "act never )
( exceeds .544", "real medians are dyn .265 / act .319 / move .141", "score>=55 averages )
( 3.6 beats vs 12.2". Every one of them is a max, a median, a count-over-threshold or a )
( conditional mean over the live corpus, and every one was QUOTED rather than re-derived, )
( which is why two of them were refuted the first time anyone recomputed them. This ROM )
( is the re-derivation: the doctrine cites a number the ROM answers, so the number cannot )
( rot without the gate going red. )
(                                                                                        )
( input  : decimal tokens on stdin, newline-terminated — T [the count threshold], then n, )
(          then n values in NON-DECREASING order. Every token must be <= 9999. )
( output : "min max med2 cnt sum mean1000" + newline, halt rc 0. )
( domain : 1 <= n <= 2343, every token <= 9999, values non-decreasing. )
(          Outside -> "NA\n" + halt rc 2. )
(                                                                                        )
( SORTED INPUT IS THE DOMAIN, NOT A CONVENIENCE. The host owns sorting — the same split )
( as spearman, where the host owns ranking and the ROM owns the formula. Sortedness buys )
( the ROM a STREAMING median: it holds two elements, not n. And the ROM VERIFIES it, so a )
( host that forgets to sort gets NA rather than a plausible wrong median. A median from )
( unsorted input is exactly the doctrine's silent-fallback shape: a real-looking number )
( that answers a different question. )
(                                                                                        )
( med2 IS TWICE THE MEDIAN, deliberately. For even n the median is the mean of the two )
( central elements and can end in .5, which an integer ROM cannot say. Halving it in the )
( host is exact; rounding it here would be a lie the caller could not see. med2 = )
( v[(n-1)/2] + v[n/2] — for odd n both indices are the same element, so it is 2*v. )
(                                                                                        )
( mean1000 is ROUNDED, not truncated — spearman learned that the hard way: truncation )
( costs exactly 1 in the last place and made the ROM disagree with its 64-bit twin on 2 )
( of 11 live windows. A fourth fractional digit decides. )
(                                                                                        )
( THE SUM IS WHY arith32 EXISTS HERE: 2343 values of 9999 sum to 23,428,257 — nine times )
( past a 16-bit word. A 16-bit accumulator would not error, it would wrap, and the mean )
( would come back small and believable. )
(                                                                                        )
( zero page: acc=00 T=02 n=04 state=06 idx=08 vmin=0a vmax=0c cnt=0e prev=10 )
(            m1=12 m2=14 loi=16 hii=18 started=1c ptr=1e pdig=20 place=22 q=24 tmp=26 )
(            fcnt=28 val=2a · 40..5f = arith32.tal's register file )
(            SUM=60/62  R32=68/6a  P32=6c/6e  PV=70/72   [all HI/LO double-word] )

|0100                        ( reset vector )
    ;on-console #10 DEO2     ( install Console/vector )
    BRK

@on-console
    #12 DEI                  ( Console/read -> byte )
    DUP #0a EQU ,&nl JCN
    DUP #30 LTH ,&bad JCN    ( a non-digit byte is not a token, it is a host bug )
    DUP #39 GTH ,&bad JCN
    #30 SUB
    #00 SWP                  ( promote to short )
    #00 LDZ2 #03e7 GTH2 ,&over JCN   ( acc > 999 before *10 -> the token exceeds 9999 )
    #00 LDZ2 #000a MUL2 ADD2 #00 STZ2
    BRK
    &over POP2 ;na JMP2      ( a complete guard: the check is BEFORE the multiply wraps )
    &bad  POP  ;na JMP2
    &nl   POP  ;token JMP2

@token
    #06 LDZ #00 EQU ,&t JCN
    #06 LDZ #01 EQU ,&n JCN
    ;got-val JMP2
    &t ;got-t JMP2
    &n ;got-n JMP2

@got-t ( the first token is the count threshold )
    #00 LDZ2 #02 STZ2
    #0000 #00 STZ2
    #01 #06 STZ
    BRK

@got-n ( the second token is n )
    #00 LDZ2 #04 STZ2
    #0000 #00 STZ2
    #04 LDZ2 #0001 LTH2 #00 EQU ,&g1 JCN
    ;na JMP2                             ( n < 1: nothing to reduce )
    &g1
    #04 LDZ2 #0927 GTH2 #00 EQU ,&g2 JCN
    ;na JMP2                             ( n > 2343: past the 32-bit accumulation ceiling )
    &g2
    #0000 #60 STZ2 #0000 #62 STZ2        ( SUM = 0 )
    #0000 #08 STZ2                       ( idx = 0 )
    #0000 #0e STZ2                       ( cnt = 0 )
    #0000 #10 STZ2                       ( prev = 0 )
    #0000 #0a STZ2 #0000 #0c STZ2        ( vmin, vmax )
    #0000 #12 STZ2 #0000 #14 STZ2        ( m1, m2 )
    #04 LDZ2 #0001 SUB2 #0002 DIV2 #16 STZ2   ( loi = (n-1)/2 )
    #04 LDZ2 #0002 DIV2 #18 STZ2              ( hii = n/2   — equal when n is odd )
    #02 #06 STZ                          ( state = 2: the rest of the tokens are values )
    BRK

@got-val
    #00 LDZ2 #2a STZ2
    #0000 #00 STZ2
    #08 LDZ2 #0000 EQU2 ,&first JCN
    #2a LDZ2 #10 LDZ2 LTH2 #00 EQU ,&ord JCN
    ;na JMP2                             ( v < prev: the input is not sorted )
    &first
    #2a LDZ2 #0a STZ2                    ( vmin = the first element )
    &ord
    #2a LDZ2 #0c STZ2                    ( vmax = the last element seen )
    #2a LDZ2 #02 LDZ2 LTH2 ,&nocnt JCN
    #0e LDZ2 INC2 #0e STZ2               ( cnt += (v >= T) )
    &nocnt
    #60 LDZ2 #40 STZ2 #62 LDZ2 #42 STZ2  ( A = SUM )
    #0000 #44 STZ2 #2a LDZ2 #46 STZ2     ( B = v )
    ;w-add JSR2
    #40 LDZ2 #60 STZ2 #42 LDZ2 #62 STZ2  ( SUM = A + v, carried into the high word )
    #08 LDZ2 #16 LDZ2 NEQ2 ,&nm1 JCN
    #2a LDZ2 #12 STZ2                    ( m1 = v[loi] )
    &nm1
    #08 LDZ2 #18 LDZ2 NEQ2 ,&nm2 JCN
    #2a LDZ2 #14 STZ2                    ( m2 = v[hii] )
    &nm2
    #2a LDZ2 #10 STZ2                    ( prev = v )
    #08 LDZ2 INC2 #08 STZ2
    #08 LDZ2 #04 LDZ2 EQU2 ,&done JCN
    BRK
    &done ;report JMP2

@report
    #0a LDZ2 ;pr16 JSR2 ;sp JSR2         ( min )
    #0c LDZ2 ;pr16 JSR2 ;sp JSR2         ( max )
    #12 LDZ2 #14 LDZ2 ADD2 ;pr16 JSR2 ;sp JSR2   ( med2 = v[loi] + v[hii] )
    #0e LDZ2 ;pr16 JSR2 ;sp JSR2         ( cnt )
    #60 LDZ2 #70 STZ2 #62 LDZ2 #72 STZ2
    ;pr32 JSR2 ;sp JSR2                  ( sum )
    ;calc-mean JSR2
    ;pr32 JSR2                           ( mean*1000, rounded )
    #0a #18 DEO
    #80 #0f DEO              ( System/state: halt, exit 0 )
    BRK

( mean*1000 without ever forming 1000*SUM — that product reaches 2.3e10 and would leave )
( 32 bits, so the integer part is divided out first and only the REMAINDER is scaled. )
( The remainder is < n <= 2343, so r*10 fits a single word and the fractional digits are )
( plain 16-bit arithmetic. Long division by decimal place costs at most 9 subtractions )
( per place instead of q of them. )
@calc-mean ( -- ; PV = round(1000*SUM/n) )
    #60 LDZ2 #68 STZ2 #62 LDZ2 #6a STZ2   ( R32 = SUM )
    #0000 #24 STZ2                        ( q = 0 )
    #03e8 #22 STZ2                        ( place = 1000 )
    &ploop
    #04 LDZ2 #4c STZ2 #22 LDZ2 #4e STZ2
    ;w-mul16 JSR2                         ( A = n*place, widened — n*1000 needs 22 bits )
    #40 LDZ2 #6c STZ2 #42 LDZ2 #6e STZ2   ( P32 = A )
    #0000 #20 STZ2                        ( pdig = 0 )
    &sloop
    #68 LDZ2 #40 STZ2 #6a LDZ2 #42 STZ2
    #6c LDZ2 #44 STZ2 #6e LDZ2 #46 STZ2
    ;w-cmp JSR2 #00 EQU ,&sdone JCN       ( R32 >= P32 ? )
    ;w-sub JSR2
    #40 LDZ2 #68 STZ2 #42 LDZ2 #6a STZ2
    #20 LDZ2 INC2 #20 STZ2                ( the count of subtractions IS the digit )
    ,&sloop JMP
    &sdone
    #24 LDZ2 #000a MUL2 #20 LDZ2 ADD2 #24 STZ2   ( q = q*10 + pdig )
    #22 LDZ2 #000a DIV2 #22 STZ2
    #22 LDZ2 #0000 NEQ2 ,&ploop JCN
    #0000 #40 STZ2 #24 LDZ2 #42 STZ2      ( A = q, the integer part )
    #0003 #28 STZ2
    &floop
    ;fdigit JSR2
    #20 LDZ2 ;w-accdigit JSR2             ( A = A*10 + digit )
    #28 LDZ2 #0001 SUB2 #28 STZ2
    #28 LDZ2 #0000 NEQ2 ,&floop JCN
    ;fdigit JSR2                          ( one more digit, only to decide the rounding )
    #20 LDZ2 #0005 LTH2 ,&noround JCN
    #0000 #44 STZ2 #0001 #46 STZ2
    ;w-add JSR2
    &noround
    #40 LDZ2 #70 STZ2 #42 LDZ2 #72 STZ2   ( PV = A )
    JMP2r

( One fractional digit of R32/n. Requires R32 < n <= 2343, which the place loop above )
( guarantees, so the whole step stays in one word and never touches A or B. )
@fdigit ( -- ; pdig = (R*10)/n, R = (R*10)%n )
    #6a LDZ2 #000a MUL2 #26 STZ2                    ( tmp = R*10, < 23430 )
    #26 LDZ2 #04 LDZ2 DIV2 #20 STZ2                 ( pdig = tmp/n )
    #26 LDZ2 #20 LDZ2 #04 LDZ2 MUL2 SUB2 #6a STZ2   ( R = tmp - pdig*n )
    JMP2r

@sp ( -- )
    #20 #18 DEO
    JMP2r

@pr16 ( v* -- )
    #72 STZ2 #0000 #70 STZ2
    ;pr32 JSR2
    JMP2r

( A 32-bit decimal printer: subtract each power of ten as a double word and count. The )
( place table is DATA, so the printer has no 32-bit constants inlined and no divide. )
@pr32 ( -- ; prints PV, consuming it )
    #00 #1c STZ                           ( started = 0 — leading-zero suppression )
    ;places #1e STZ2
    &ploop
    #1e LDZ2 LDA2 #44 STZ2                ( Bhi = place hi )
    #1e LDZ2 #0002 ADD2 LDA2 #46 STZ2     ( Blo = place lo )
    #0000 #20 STZ2
    &sloop
    #70 LDZ2 #40 STZ2 #72 LDZ2 #42 STZ2
    ;w-cmp JSR2 #00 EQU ,&sdone JCN
    ;w-sub JSR2
    #40 LDZ2 #70 STZ2 #42 LDZ2 #72 STZ2
    #20 LDZ2 INC2 #20 STZ2
    ,&sloop JMP
    &sdone
    #20 LDZ2 #0000 NEQ2 ,&emit JCN
    #1c LDZ #00 NEQ ,&emit JCN
    #1e LDZ2 ;places-last EQU2 ,&emit JCN ( the units place always prints )
    ,&next JMP
    &emit
    #01 #1c STZ
    #20 LDZ2 NIP #30 ADD #18 DEO
    &next
    #1e LDZ2 #0004 ADD2 #1e STZ2
    #1e LDZ2 ;places-end LTH2 #00 EQU ,&fin JCN
    ;pr32/ploop JMP2         ( ten places is more than a relative branch can reach back )
    &fin
    JMP2r

@na
    ;na-str ;emit JSR2
    #82 #0f DEO              ( halt, exit 2 — honest domain n/a, never a wrapped verdict )
    BRK

@emit ( str* -- )
    &loop
    LDAk #00 EQU ,&done JCN
    LDAk #18 DEO
    INC2 ,&loop JMP
    &done
    POP2
    JMP2r

@na-str  "NA 0a 00

@places
    3b9a ca00    ( 1000000000 )
    05f5 e100    (  100000000 )
    0098 9680    (   10000000 )
    000f 4240    (    1000000 )
    0001 86a0    (     100000 )
    0000 2710    (      10000 )
    0000 03e8    (       1000 )
    0000 0064    (        100 )
    0000 000a    (         10 )
@places-last
    0000 0001    (          1 )
@places-end

~arith32.tal
